# ProofOwl frontend — configuration
#
# EVERY value in this file is PUBLIC: a contract id, an RPC URL, a
# network passphrase. They are safe to commit and safe to ship to the
# browser (that is what the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix does, and it is correct
# here — on-chain reads run client-side).
#
# This repo MUST NEVER contain a private key of any kind — no
# ATTESTOR_SECRET_KEY, no wallet seed, no keystore. It is a public,
# client-side app that only simulates reads and asks a wallet extension
# for its public address. There is no server-side signing path to hold a
# secret for. See the README "Security" section.
#
# All three have working defaults baked into src/lib/config.ts, so the
# app runs with no .env at all. Override only to point at a different
# instance.

# v0.3 (crate 0.3.0) testnet instance — proofowl-contracts README
# "Deployed contracts" table. Marked "disposable; may be replaced".
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROOFOWL_CONTRACT_ID=CAIDTSVPQICTA2VLE6BSQYHEELHGPZWQDYWKSDBRW4LYPZH6Q44UTAOA

# Soroban RPC endpoint. Must be https://.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROOFOWL_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org

# Network passphrase the RPC serves. The Stellar mainnet passphrase is
# rejected at startup — this is a read-only testnet explorer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROOFOWL_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE=Test SDF Network ; September 2015
